# docs/calibration/SI3-PROVISIONAL.log — @pixagram/paph-x 1.1.2
#
# The 1.1.2 runs: the Pixa chain's artworks at one snapshot, and the synthetic corpus under SI3
# and SI2. Quoted by docs/SPEC-SI-paph-si.md (§0, §4.3, §5.4, §9.5, §9.7, §10, §11),
# docs/PAPH-X.md (§2, §4 — its last subsection — §6), docs/SEARCH.md, the README, the CHANGELOG
# and integrations/pixagram-search/README.md.
# Native, one core of a shared two-core container (Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.10GHz); rust/target/release/sibench,
# run from rust/. Timings move by a few percent between runs, and more when the host is busy;
# everything else is deterministic and reproduces exactly from the same snapshot.
#
# The snapshot (0): node tools/chain-corpus.mjs, which wrote rust/target/chain-corpus — the RGBA
# images, manifest.jsonl (manifest sha256 8d06cb4711e0e1e9c43dabe50edf3ed11039975a17dbc9bfec0afcf1dd27c055),
# index.tsv and snapshot.json. The images are not in the repository; a later run of the tool reads
# a later snapshot.
#
# docs/calibration/SI3-PROVISIONAL.psi was written by run 3 without --out; here run 3 writes a
# copy, and the sha256 lines at the end show it equal to the committed file, as runs 12a and 12b
# reproduce SI2 and SI1. Then the lines of the unit tests that print a result.

